From: Growth Habitat build assistant
Subject: [PATCH] Conversations: three-step form, card list, live wiring

Patch 04. The evidence-collection floor goes live. Conversations is now a
fully working surface — log them, edit them, see them surface on the
Command Center.

Files modified
--------------
src/App.tsx — Adds /conversations and /conversations/:id routes.
src/components/Primitives.tsx — Adds five new primitives:
  - ChipMultiSelect for tagging energy gains/drains
  - SegmentedSelect for trust signal, evidence strength, work-with checks
  - CheckboxRow for market pull signals
  - StepIndicator for the multi-step form navigation
  - onClick prop added to existing Tile component
src/pages/CommandCenter.tsx — Wires "Add talk" button to create a blank
  conversation and navigate to its editor. Strongest direction tile and
  best conversation tile are now clickable. Empty-state best conversation
  tile click also creates a new conversation.

Files added
-----------
src/components/ConversationForm.tsx — Multi-step form with autosave on every
  field. Step 1: who/when (person, org, role, date, related direction,
  evidence strength). Step 2: energy & signal (energy before/after, five
  Buffett-lens scores, trust signal three-state, work-with-on-hard-problem
  yes/maybe/no). Step 3: insight & follow-up (key insight, six market pull
  checkboxes, energy gain/drain tags pulled from Profile, free notes,
  follow-up action). Step indicator at top supports clicking to jump.

src/components/ConversationCard.tsx — Single card row for the list view.
  Shows person, org/role, energy gain as a chip, evidence strength,
  key insight as a serif pull-quote, follow-up action, related direction,
  date, signal average. Hover effect, click to edit.

src/pages/Conversations.tsx — List page. Sorted most-recent-first.
  Empty state copy: "Conversations are experiments. Log them within
  24 hours — memory edits the data."

src/pages/Conversation.tsx — Single conversation editor page wrapping
  the multi-step form. Crumbs show person name, breadcrumb back to
  list, quiet saving indicator in topbar.

Data shape
----------
The Conversation type was already in place from patch 03. This patch only
uses existing fields. Market pull signals are stored as a prefix tag in
the notes field for now: `[market_pull:asked_for_followup,introduced_me] ...`
The form transparently handles this prefix; the user sees clean notes.
A typed marketPull[] field will be promoted in patch 04b alongside
Opportunities — a schema migration, not done in this patch to keep scope
tight.

UX decisions
------------
- Three-step flow (not single long form). Lighter cognitive load when
  logging right after a conversation. Steps autosave per-field, so
  abandoning mid-flow doesn't lose data.
- Card list (not table). Each conversation is an artifact, not a row.
- Empty state is the page (not an onboarding CTA). The product instructs
  through being itself.
- Date defaults to today. Reduces friction for the 90% case.
- Quick-add: clicking "Add talk" creates a blank conversation immediately
  and navigates to its editor. No modal, no in-between state.

Apply with:
    git apply 0004-conversations.patch

Or with plain patch:
    patch -p1 < 0004-conversations.patch

Verify:
    npm run build
    npm run dev

Then in the browser:
1. Click "03 Talks" in the sidebar — empty state appears
2. Click "Log your first conversation" — multi-step form appears
3. Fill step 1, click Continue — step 2 appears, data persists
4. Fill some scores, click back — step 1 still has your data
5. Click step 3 directly via the step indicator — it works
6. Click "Save & close" — back at the list, your conversation is there
7. Click the card — back into the editor
8. Go to Command Center — best conversation tile shows your entry
9. Click the tile — opens the conversation

